#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
vaultsync — two-way mirror between a local vault folder and Google Drive.

Two modes per folder:
  files — plain files both ways, driven by `rclone bisync`
  docs  — each note lives in Drive as a native Google Doc you can share and
          comment on, driven by the Drive API directly

Both modes give you:
  - newest-timestamp-wins conflict resolution, so folders stay clean, except
    for shared Docs, where both versions are kept instead
  - a browsable version history, so anything overwritten or deleted is
    archived rather than destroyed
  - a per-folder background daemon (FSEvents watch + interval poll) run by
    launchd, under an interpreter macOS allows to read ~/Documents

Run `vaultsync help` for usage.
"""

